### 4. File and Folder Creation / Renaming Patterns

From `D:\My Drive\My Obsidian Vault\Main_03\.obsidian\plugins\obsidian-hazard-trigger\src\utils\componentManager.ts`:

#### Path Resolution
```typescript
public static resolveFullPath(relPath: string): string {
  const clean = normalizePath(relPath).replace(/\\/g, '/');
  if (clean.startsWith('Hazard_Trigger_Data/')) return clean;
  if (clean.startsWith('Matrices/')) return normalizePath(`Hazard_Trigger_Data/${clean}`).replace(/\\/g, '/');
  return normalizePath(`Hazard_Trigger_Data/Components/${clean}`).replace(/\\/g, '/');
}
```

#### Component File Creation
```typescript
public static async createComponentFile(
  app: App,
  folderRelPath: string,
  fileName: string,
  displayName?: string
): Promise<string | null> {
  const adapter = app.vault.adapter;
  const sanitizedFileName = fileName.endsWith('.json') ? fileName : `${fileName}.json`;
  const folderPath = this.resolveFullPath(folderRelPath);
  const targetFilePath = normalizePath(`${folderPath}/${sanitizedFileName}`).replace(/\\/g, '/');

  try {
    if (!(await adapter.exists(folderPath))) {
      await adapter.mkdir(folderPath);
    }
    if (await adapter.exists(targetFilePath)) {
      return targetFilePath;
    }
    await adapter.write(targetFilePath, JSON.stringify({}, null, 2));
    return targetFilePath;
  } catch (err) {
    console.error(`[ComponentManager] Failed to create file at ${targetFilePath}:`, err);
    return null;
  }
}
```

#### Option Entry Renaming and Updating (Inside JSON Files)
Option key renaming is handled in `ComponentManager.saveEntry`:
```typescript
public static async saveEntry(
  app: App,
  fileRelPath: string,
  newKey: string,
  entryData: ComponentEntry,
  oldKey?: string
): Promise<boolean> {
  const adapter = app.vault.adapter;
  const targetPath = this.resolveFullPath(fileRelPath);
  let existingEntries: Record<string, ComponentEntry> = {};

  if (await adapter.exists(targetPath)) {
    const raw = await adapter.read(targetPath);
    existingEntries = JSON.parse(raw);
  }

  // Renaming support: delete old key if key was modified
  if (oldKey && oldKey !== newKey && existingEntries[oldKey] !== undefined) {
    delete existingEntries[oldKey];
  }

  existingEntries[newKey] = this.sanitizeEntry(entryData);
  // Sanitize remaining entries and write back formatted JSON
  ...
  await adapter.write(targetPath, JSON.stringify(sanitizedEntries, null, 2));
  return true;
}
```

#### Batch File Table Commit
`ComponentManager.saveAllFileEntries(app, fileRelPath, entries)` ensures the parent directory exists via `adapter.mkdir()`, sanitizes all entries with `sanitizeEntry()`, and writes the entire JSON file in one operation.

#### File & Folder Management Status
- **File level creation:** Exists via `ComponentManager.createComponentFile`.
- **Option level renaming / deletion:** Exists via `ComponentManager.saveEntry` (with `oldKey`) and `ComponentManager.deleteEntry`.
- **File/Folder level renaming / deletion:** `renameComponentFile`, `deleteComponentFile`, `createFolder`, `renameFolder`, and `deleteFolder` are not yet implemented in `componentManager.ts`.
